; An INLINE map carrying a group choice (`{ x: uint // y: tstr }`) used as a member/element type
; panics parsing (`group choices in inlined map types not allowed`, parsing.rs) — a DISTINCT site
; from the plain anonymous-composite "Anonymous groups not allowed" panic (which fires for choice-
; free inline maps): the group-choice check trips first. The named form (`t = { x: uint // y: tstr }`
; referenced by name) is the supported spelling. No matrix cell covers a group-choice-map in member
; position (contain.* map cells are choice-free), so this hand fixture is the pin. Surfaced by the
; recombination sweep (src/tests/recombination_tests.rs).
a = [{ x: uint // y: tstr }]
